/-!
# Linear disjointness from the perfect closure and `p`-th roots of a transcendental

Let `k ⊆ F ⊆ E` be fields.

* `LinearIndependent.algebraMap_perfectClosure`: if `F ⊗_k k^{perf}` is reduced, where
  `k^{perf}` is the perfect closure of `k` in `E` (e.g. if `F / k` is separably generated), then
  every `k`-linearly independent family of `F` stays linearly independent over `k^{perf}` in `E`.
* `Algebra.isSeparablyGenerated_of_transcendental` and
  `LinearIndependent.algebraMap_perfectClosure_of_transcendental`: the same when `F` is separable
  algebraic over `k(x)` for some `x` transcendental over `k`.
* `sum_mul_pow_ne_algebraMap`: if `x ∈ F` is transcendental over `k` and `F` is separable
  algebraic over `k(x)`, then (in characteristic `p`) `x` is not the `p`-th power of an element
  of the ring generated by `k^{perf}` and `F` in `E`.
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped TensorProduct IntermediateField

open Polynomial IntermediateField

variable {k F E : Type*} [Field k] [Field F] [Field E] [Algebra k F] [Algebra k E] [Algebra F E]
  [IsScalarTower k F E]

